{"plan_objective_id": 1, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 1,
  "objective": "Research bright particles in LPBF AlSi10Mg: Fe-rich intermetallics, Si particles, oxides, and contaminants - BSE contrast and EDS signatures",
  "rationale": "Key evidence gathered: Fe-rich intermetallics appear bright in BSE (Z=26 vs 13 for Al), cell spacing 0.5-0.9 um, Fe content <0.55 wt%, Fe segregates to boundaries",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Fe-rich intermetallics are bright in BSE due to higher Z (Fe=26). Typical Fe <0.55 wt%. Oxides have lower Z and appear dark. Si is similar Z to Al, subtle contrast. Embedded abrasives possible but explained by literature.",
  "evaluation": "Multiple primary sources confirm Fe-rich intermetallic BSE brightness and typical alloy composition"
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 2, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 2,
  "objective": "Research cellular network in LPBF AlSi10Mg: Si-rich eutectic boundaries, cell size, BSE contrast, and polishing relief effects",
  "rationale": "Cell size 0.5-0.9 um confirmed. Si-rich boundaries ~29.6 wt% Si. BSE contrast confirmed from Z-number difference. Polishing relief documented.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Cell spacing 0.5-0.9 um matches user observation of 0.5-0.8 um. Si-rich boundaries have ~29.6 wt% Si. Si (Z=14) vs Al (Z=13) gives subtle BSE contrast, enhanced by polishing relief on napped cloth.",
  "evaluation": "Multiple sources confirm cell spacing and Si enrichment at boundaries"
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 3, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 3,
  "objective": "Research dark spots: diamond embedding in aluminum, pores/pits from polishing, Mg2Si/oxide contrast in BSE",
  "rationale": "Diamond embedding documented for soft metals including indium and aluminum. Dark spots consistent with multiple candidates.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Diamond embedding in soft metals is well documented (Geller 2002). Oxides have lower Z than Al and appear dark. Mg2Si has similar/lower Z. Nanopores also dark. Diamond (Z=6) would be very dark in BSE.",
  "evaluation": "Key references confirm diamond embedding risk and BSE contrast behavior"
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 4, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 4,
  "objective": "Research EDS conditions for sub-micron particle analysis in Al matrix: interaction volume, low-kV analysis, standards",
  "rationale": "Berger 2014 and Hovington/CASINO provide relevant guidance. Need to synthesize for 5 kV and 15 kV in Al.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "At 5 kV in Al, interaction volume ~0.3 um diameter. At 15 kV, ~2.5 um. Low kV needed for sub-micron particles. FEG-EPMA resolution ~200 nm at 5 kV. Standards should be matched to candidate phases.",
  "evaluation": "Monte Carlo simulation data and EPMA resolution measurements provide quantitative guidance"
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 5, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 5,
  "objective": "Research embedded abrasive contamination from metallographic preparation (alumina, SiC, diamond) in soft metals",
  "rationale": "Geller 2002 and Rémond 2002 and MacKenzie 2005 all document embedding. Now need to compile.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Alumina, SiC, diamond, and silica can all embed in soft metals. Geller warns that indium was full of 0.1 um diamond. MacKenzie notes diamond embedding in aluminum specifically. Alumina was used but would appear dark in BSE not bright.",
  "evaluation": "Three key references document embedding mechanisms"
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 6, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 6,
  "objective": "Create artifacts summarizing findings and provide final comprehensive answer",
  "rationale": "All evidence gathered. Need to create summary table and submit answer.",
  "status": "in-progress",
  "result": null,
  "evaluation": null
}"}

